 attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a detail is uncertain, identify what source you would need next. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new evidence. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Transfer to a new inquiry"}],"title":"Year 3, Week 1, Lesson 2: Mapping our local area","unit_number":1,"unit_title":"Our local community and its history","week":1,"week_in_unit":1,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nExample map \"Home to the park\": a square symbol marks home, a green patch marks the park and S marks the shop. Oak Street runs north to south and the north arrow points to the top. The key says square = home, green = park, S = shop.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the sources, places or community details used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"A map is a plan from above, not a side picture.","caption":"Plan view shows where things are.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Map</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">view from above</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Photo</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">side view of houses</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Key symbols and north arrow on a sketch map.","caption":"Title, key and north arrow make a map usable.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill